.if n .if \n[LL]>80n .nr LL 80n
.if n .if \n[LT]>80n .nr LT 80n
.TH ISOCMD.CONF 5 "November 2026" "Iso Commander 8.0.41"
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
isocmd.conf \- configuration file for Iso Commander
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration file is
.IR ~/.config/isocmd/config .
Settings use the form
.IR "key = value" .
Lines beginning with # are comments. Numeric settings accept non-negative
integers without signs, decimal points or leading zeros, within the
ranges below. Missing or invalid settings are replaced with defaults.
.PP
Most settings take effect immediately when changed in the interactive
settings editor. The global thread pool limit requires a restart;
automatic database updates are a startup setting.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Appearance settings
.TP
.B base
Default state and input color.
Values: ash, black, charcoal, gray, silver, steel, white.
Default: white.
.TP
.B skin
Menu and header color.
Values: amber, black, cyan, gray, green, purple, rose, white.
Default: white.
.TP
.B theme
Color palette for lists and prompts.
Values: classic, crimson, dracula, forest, high_contrast, midnight, mono,
neon, ocean, original, paper, retro, sakura, sunset, tokyo.
Default: original.
.SS General settings
.TP
.B auto_update
Refresh the ISO database on startup using folder path history.
Values: on, off. Default: off.
.TP
.B filenames_only
Display filenames instead of full paths, except in the unmount list.
Values: on, off. Default: off.
.TP
.B pagination
Items per page (0 disables pagination).
Range: 0\-1000. Default: 25.
.SS Write2USB settings
.TP
.B verify_checksum
Verify USB write integrity using CRC-64 in interactive mode.
Values: on, off. Default: off.
.TP
.B buffered_writes
Use buffered I/O for Windows and WinPE writes in both modes.
Values: on, off. Default: on.
.SS History settings
.TP
.B folder_path_history_lines
Maximum unique folder paths to persist (0 disables history).
Range: 0\-5000. Default: 30.
.TP
.B filter_history_lines
Maximum unique search filters to persist (0 disables history).
Range: 0\-1000. Default: 15.
.SS Display modes
All list display settings accept full or compact. Filename-only display
overrides these settings, except for the unmount list.
.TP
.B mount_list
Mount operations. Default: compact.
.TP
.B umount_list
Unmount operations. Default: full.
.TP
.B cp_mv_rm_list
Copy, move and delete operations. Default: full.
.TP
.B write2usb_list
USB writing. Default: compact.
.TP
.B convert2iso_lists
Image conversion. Default: compact.
.SS Thread configuration
A shared thread pool uses the reported hardware concurrency (at least 2)
capped by combined_thread_cap. Sub-limits draw from this pool; tasks queue
when workers are unavailable.
.TP
.B combined_thread_cap
Global thread pool limit (requires restart).
Range: 1\-256. Default: 16.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_mount
Maximum concurrent mounting tasks.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 8.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_umount
Maximum concurrent unmounting tasks.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 8.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_cp_mv
Maximum concurrent copy or move tasks.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 4.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_rm
Maximum concurrent file removal tasks.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 8.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_convert2iso
Maximum concurrent ISO conversions.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 4.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_database_cleanup
Maximum threads for ISO database cleanup.
Range: 1\-128. Default: 4.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_list_sorting
Maximum threads for list sorting.
Range: 1\-64. Default: 2.
.TP
.B thread_cap_for_list_filtering
Maximum threads for list filtering.
Range: 1\-64. Default: 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/isocmd/config
User configuration file. With sudo, HOME is normally /root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR isocmd (1)
